* sg13g2-bandgap -- closed-loop vref/TC PEX bench body for the `klt sim`
* harness (issue #278, the remaining half of #275). Instantiated by
* sim/closed-loop-vref-pvt-pex/run_klt_sim.sh, which substitutes @@OSDI_DIR@@,
* @@VDD@@ (per supply -- the ramp's target is part of the fixture, so the
* supply axis cannot ride the request's `alter` channel the way the core
* bench's plain DC rail does) and @@PEX_BODY@@. The DUT half -- every
* device and every wire parasitic of the ASSEMBLED block (bandgap_core +
* bandgap_amp + bandgap_startup, exactly as design/bandgap_top.sch wires
* them) -- is GENERATED by `sim/tools/gen_pex_netlist_body.py --cell top`
* and rides in through the include; nothing here transcribes an extraction
* card. Edit the fixture here, the DUT in the generator's two committed
* inputs.
*
* `klt sim` netlist-body convention: this file is a circuit BODY. No
* `.lib`, no `.temp`, no `.options temp=`, no analysis card, no `.end`.
*
* ONE DELIBERATE DEVIATION, same as every `klt sim` body in this repo: the
* `.control` block below (SG13G2's OSDI compact models must be loaded by
* `pre_osdi` before the netlist is parsed; filed upstream,
* klayout-tools#2666 -- see sim/harness/README.md "Upstream friction").
.control
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/psp103.osdi
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/psp103_nqs.osdi
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/mosvar.osdi
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/r3_cmc.osdi
.endc

* Solver options. `reltol=5e-3` is the settled trim-bearing setting. The
* hand-transcribed template's convergence aids `rshunt=1e9`/`gmin=1e-9` are
* deliberately ABSENT -- issue #278 drops them: against the ladder's
* interior nodes they leak ~0.55 uA out of the output branch, a ~37 mV
* settled-vref artifact at code 128. The supply ramp below is the
* convergence path that replaces them.
.options reltol=5e-3

* Resident-vector save (issue #278 work item 3): the refreshed top
* extraction is 261 nets before the parasitic hub nodes, and a 3 ms
* transient at the default all-nodes x all-timesteps allocation can trip
* ngspice's startup allocation. Every vector this bench reads is
* enumerated; nothing else needs to be resident. NOTE the consequence,
* verified on ngspice 46: a `.save` list disables `par('...')` inside
* `.meas ... find` (the expression is rewritten to an internal `pa_<n>`
* parameter that is then not a resident vector), so the two derived
* columns (dvsns_v, vref_settle_delta_v) are formed by the runner from the
* reported operands -- the same practice this experiment's committed
* records already use for their derived columns.
.save v(fb) v(sns1) v(sns2) v(det) v(vref) v(cb3) i(Vmkfb)

* FIXTURE -- transient supply ramp: vdd ramps 0 -> VDD over 200 us and
* holds to 3 ms, the same shape sim/closed-loop-vref-pvt uses, so vref can
* be measured at two separated time points (2 ms, 3 ms) and confirmed
* settled. @@VDD@@ is substituted per supply by the runner: the PWL source
* is the one rail shape `alter` would clobber, so the supply axis lives in
* per-supply body variants, not in the request.
Vvdd vdd 0 PWL(0 0 200u @@VDD@@ 3m @@VDD@@)
Vvss vss 0 dc 0

* Ground reference for the extracted wire capacitances: the extraction
* itself carries its own 1 TOhm DC-only tie (`rvsubs_dctie vsubs 0 1e+12`
* rides in the generated wire-parasitic block) -- correct for a transient
* bench and nothing extra is needed here.

* DUT -- generated PEX body for bandgap_top (17 MOS legs, XR1/XR2/XRPU,
* the 255-unit ladder under its XRU<n> names, XQ1-XQ3 spliced from the
* design netlists, the Vmkfb drain split this bench measures
* i(Vmkfb) through, and every wire parasitic).
.include @@PEX_BODY@@
